{"Title":"An Act to prevent unwanted opioid prescriptions","BillNumber":"H1801","DocketNumber":"HD2134","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"AXV1","Name":"Andres X. Vargas","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AXV1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T09:06:14.9"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"AXV1","Name":"Andres X. Vargas","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AXV1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T09:06:14.9166667"},{"Id":"K_D1","Name":"Kate Donaghue","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/K_D1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T10:46:47.9966667"}],"JointSponsor":{"Id":"K_D1","Name":"Kate Donaghue","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/K_D1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T19:11:48.437"},"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1801/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representatives Vargas of Haverhill and Donaghue of Westborough, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1801) of Andres X. Vargas and Kate Donaghue relative to the penalty for the issuance of unwanted opioid prescriptions.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSubsection (e) of section 18B of chapter 94C of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following 2 sentences:-\r\n\tA practitioner who knowingly fails to comply with a person’s voluntary non-opiate directive form shall be subject to a civil penalty of not more than $100,000. The attorney general may enforce the provisions of this subsection.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}